                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>This course is a required professional course designed for students in the eight-year clinical medicine program. Its main content includes an overview of human morphology, the history, research methods, and recent advancements in morphological studies; the structure and function of epithelial tissues, intrinsic connective tissues, cartilage, bone, blood, muscle tissue, and nervous tissue; the structure of the skin and its appendages; and early embryonic development. It serves as a solid foundation for further study in other basic medical and clinical medicine courses.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
